==Battleground==
*6 [[Coffin Zoge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Zamelle]] spawns as the boss after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*3 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is the only [[Growing Strange]] stage where the boss comes out on a timer; for this reason, luring or delaying is a bad idea, especially because the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] may take down your base by burrowing (Zamelle does not burrow, but she has Base Destroyer).

Due to the introduction of [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] this stage has become much more manageable, as he can get rid of Coffin Zoges and Zamelles with complete ease, while also having slow immunity to counter Zomboe. He won't hold up well versus Zang Roo, though (unless at very high levels), so you might want to summon another unit for them, such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]. Otherwise, at Lv.40+ he can basically solo this stage on his own.

Do not bring [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] for this stage as it will be outranged by Zang Roo and is not as effective as other options. Its cost also renders it a waste of cash.

